<!DOCTYPE score-partwise PUBLIC "-//Recordare//DTD MusicXML 3.0 Partwise//EN" "http://www.musicxml.org/dtds/partwise.dtd">
<score-partwise>
  <work>
    <work-title>Come Forth! Come On, with Solemn Song!</work-title>
  </work>
  <identification>
    <creator type="composer">Words: Christian Friedrich Heinrich Sachse, 1849.  Translated by Jane Borthwick, 1855.
Music: 'Jeg Har Min Sag Til Gud Hjemstilt' or 'My All I To My God Commend'
Ludvig Mathias Lindeman, unknown date.
Setting: The Lutheran Hymnary, 1913.
copyright: public domain.  This score is a part of the Open Hymnal Project, 2026 Revision.</creator>
    <encoding>
      <encoder>abc2xml version 268</encoder>
      <software>https://wim.vree.org/svgParse/abc2xml.html</software>
      <encoding-date>2026-09-07</encoding-date>
    </encoding>
    <source>Music source: "The Lutheran Hymnary", 1913 Hymn 481
Lyrics source: "Hymns from the Land of Luther", 1858 Hymn 54</source>
    <miscellaneous>
      <miscellaneous-field name="lyrics">6. How many graves around us lie!
How many homes are in the sky!
Yes, for each saint doth Christ prepare
A place with care:
Thy home is waiting, brother, there!

7. Jesus, Thou reignest, Lord alone,
Thou wilt return and claim Thine own,
Come quickly, Lord! return again!
Amen! Amen!
Thine seal us ever, now and then!</miscellaneous-field>
    </miscellaneous>
  </identification>
